Quack-Step Cabaret

Creative Catalyst: The genre was born during the chaotic union of the rival Zampano and Vane circus dynasties, where the brass band and the electronic producers were forced to play in tandem to drown out the guests’ bickering.

This genre is a high-octane collision of jagged, syncopated Moombahton rhythms and the virtuosic, improvisational dissonance of Jazz Rock. It is defined by "Barking Duck" sonics—a signature synthesis technique where brass samples are pitch-shifted and side-chained to create aggressive, quacking, percussive swells. The mood is manic, surreal, and deeply psychedelic, blending the grit of a dusty circus tent with the precise, trippy textures of modern bass music.

Genre DNA
*   Tempo & Pulse: 108–112 BPM, featuring a heavy, reggaeton-derived kick-snare pattern that is constantly disrupted by polyrhythmic jazz drumming.
*   Harmonic Palette: Diminished scales and Lydian dominant modes, punctuated by sharp, dissonant jazz chords and wandering, liquid basslines.
*   Production Signatures: "Duck-Gating" (side-chaining brass stabs to a sub-bass carrier), tape-saturated granular synthesis on woodwind samples, and aggressive, non-linear panning.
*   Dynamics: A constant, frantic "call and response" between tight, quantized electronic percussion and loose, chaotic live jazz solos.

Scene & Origin Lore
The subculture thrives in the "Under-Tent" districts of former industrial port cities, where performers wear velvet tuxedos patched with circuit boards and illuminated bird masks. It began when the Zampano/Vane wedding guests realized the only way to silence the rival factions was to out-play them with a sound that felt like a fever dream. Today, the scene is defined by secret, pop-up "Menagerie Raves" held in abandoned theaters, where the fashion is "Victorian-glitch"—tight corsets, goggles, and high-frequency digital displays.

Central Instruments: A modified Hohner Clavinet, an analog Korg MS-20 for "ducking" lead lines, live trumpet with a plunger mute, and a heavily processed, granularized saxophone.

For Fans Of: Flying Lotus, Mr. Bungle, Venetian Snares, Caravan Palace.

